IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mca-nouns`
IMPORT `mca-act`
IMPORT `mca-reading`

-- Minors' Contracts Act 1987 (Singapore) -- LAYER 1 TESTS.  Every expected value was written from the text
-- of the Act before the assertion was run, and is stated beside it.  Nothing here is copied from output.
-- Each rule's every branch is hit; each date boundary of ss 1 to 4 is tried on both sides (9 and 10 April
-- 1987; 11 and 12 November 1993); a case outside what the Act answers is asserted as NOTHING.
--
-- How the Act's days run.  "After 9 April 1987" is strict: a contract made ON 9 April 1987 is not after
-- it.  "Before 12 November 1993" is strict too: a contract made ON 12 November 1993 is not before it.  So
-- the band s 4 shuts out is 10 April 1987 to 11 November 1993 inclusive, and ss 1 to 3 reach (by their own
-- words) a contract made on or after 12 November 1993, or earlier if s 4's exception is met.

§ `Test fixtures`

GIVETH A DATE
`1 January 1980` MEANS Date 1 1 1980
GIVETH A DATE
`8 April 1987` MEANS Date 8 4 1987
GIVETH A DATE
`13 November 1993` MEANS Date 13 11 1993
GIVETH A DATE
`10 April 1987` MEANS Date 10 4 1987
GIVETH A DATE
`15 June 1990` MEANS Date 15 6 1990
GIVETH A DATE
`11 November 1993` MEANS Date 11 11 1993
GIVETH A DATE
`1 March 2020` MEANS Date 1 3 2020

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      minor IS A BOOLEAN
      unenforceable IS A BOOLEAN
      repudiates IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A BOOLEAN
      saving IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Contract with a minor`
`a contract with` MEANS
    `Contract with a minor` WITH
        `day the contract was made` IS day
        `one party was a minor when the contract was made` IS minor
        `the obligation is unenforceable against that party` IS JUST unenforceable
        `that party repudiates the contract` IS repudiates
        `that is because that party was a minor when the contract was made` IS JUST reason
        `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made the provision applicable` IS saving

-- A minor's contract made after 12 November 1993 in which the person does not know the law the Act presupposes.
GIVEN unenforceable IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      repudiates IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Contract with a minor`
`a contract where the law presupposed is`  MEANS
    `Contract with a minor` WITH
        `day the contract was made` IS `1 March 2020`
        `one party was a minor when the contract was made` IS TRUE
        `the obligation is unenforceable against that party` IS unenforceable
        `that party repudiates the contract` IS repudiates
        `that is because that party was a minor when the contract was made` IS reason
        `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made the provision applicable` IS NOTHING

-- A contract made after 12 November 1993 in which the reason is not known; the record says whether a party was a minor.
GIVEN minor IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Contract with a minor`
`a contract where the reason is not known and minority is` MEANS
    `Contract with a minor` WITH
        `day the contract was made` IS `1 March 2020`
        `one party was a minor when the contract was made` IS minor
        `the obligation is unenforceable against that party` IS JUST TRUE
        `that party repudiates the contract` IS FALSE
        `that is because that party was a minor when the contract was made` IS NOTHING
        `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made the provision applicable` IS NOTHING

-- The standard case: a minor, whose obligation is unenforceable because he was a minor, and who has not repudiated.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      saving IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Contract with a minor`
`the standard contract made on` MEANS
    `a contract with` day TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE saving

GIVEN contract IS A `Contract with a minor`
      given IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Guarantee case`
`a guarantee case on` MEANS
    `Guarantee case` WITH
        `the contract guaranteed` IS contract
        `a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to the contract` IS given

GIVEN contract IS A `Contract with a minor`
      entered IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Restitution case`
`a restitution case on` MEANS
    `Restitution case` WITH
        `the contract sued on` IS contract
        `the claimant entered into the contract with the defendant` IS entered

`property acquired under the contract` MEANS Property OF TRUE, FALSE
`property representing what was acquired` MEANS Property OF FALSE, TRUE
`property both acquired and representing` MEANS Property OF TRUE, TRUE
`property neither acquired nor representing` MEANS Property OF FALSE, FALSE

`an other remedy available to the claimant` MEANS Remedy OF TRUE, TRUE
`the s 3(1) transfer itself` MEANS Remedy OF FALSE, TRUE
`an other remedy not available to the claimant` MEANS Remedy OF TRUE, FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Tests -- section 4`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The band: s 4 "after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993", both ends strict.
#ASSERT `s 4 the band a contract made on a day falls in` `1 January 1980` EQUALS `made on or before 9 April 1987`
#ASSERT `s 4 the band a contract made on a day falls in` `9 April 1987` EQUALS `made on or before 9 April 1987`
#ASSERT `s 4 the band a contract made on a day falls in` `10 April 1987` EQUALS `made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993`
#ASSERT `s 4 the band a contract made on a day falls in` `15 June 1990` EQUALS `made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993`
#ASSERT `s 4 the band a contract made on a day falls in` `11 November 1993` EQUALS `made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993`
#ASSERT `s 4 the band a contract made on a day falls in` `12 November 1993` EQUALS `made on or after 12 November 1993`
#ASSERT `s 4 the band a contract made on a day falls in` `1 March 2020` EQUALS `made on or after 12 November 1993`

-- "After 9 April 1987" as a limb test, both sides of the day.
#ASSERT NOT (`the day is after 9 April 1987` `1 January 1980`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the day is after 9 April 1987` `9 April 1987`)
#ASSERT `the day is after 9 April 1987` `10 April 1987`
#ASSERT `the day is after 9 April 1987` `1 March 2020`

-- What s 4 does: in the band, the exception ("except in so far as it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909") decides.
#ASSERT `s 4 what this section does to a provision of this Act` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS `s 4 leaves this provision to section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909`
#ASSERT `s 4 what this section does to a provision of this Act` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `s 4 shuts this provision out`
#ASSERT `s 4 what this section does to a provision of this Act` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` NOTHING) EQUALS `s 4 leaves open whether section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made this provision applicable`
#ASSERT `s 4 what this section does to a provision of this Act` (`the standard contract made on` `10 April 1987` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `s 4 shuts this provision out`
#ASSERT `s 4 what this section does to a provision of this Act` (`the standard contract made on` `11 November 1993` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `s 4 shuts this provision out`
-- Outside the band s 4 does not speak, whatever the saving fact says.
#ASSERT `s 4 what this section does to a provision of this Act` (`the standard contract made on` `1 January 1980` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `s 4 does not speak to this contract`
#ASSERT `s 4 what this section does to a provision of this Act` (`the standard contract made on` `9 April 1987` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `s 4 does not speak to this contract`
#ASSERT `s 4 what this section does to a provision of this Act` (`the standard contract made on` `12 November 1993` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS `s 4 does not speak to this contract`
#ASSERT `s 4 what this section does to a provision of this Act` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS `s 4 does not speak to this contract`

-- The gate: JUST FALSE when s 4 shuts the provision out, NOTHING when it leaves it to a rule outside the sources, JUST TRUE when it does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 4 the provision of this Act is open to apply to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 the provision of this Act is open to apply to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 the provision of this Act is open to apply to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 the provision of this Act is open to apply to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 the provision of this Act is open to apply to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `9 April 1987` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 the provision of this Act is open to apply to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `12 November 1993` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The bar as its own question.  Shut: JUST TRUE.  Exception met: JUST FALSE.  Not known: NOTHING.
-- Outside the window the text names: JUST FALSE (the window is fixed in the text's own words; the bar does not reach the contract).
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `10 April 1987` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `11 November 1993` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `9 April 1987` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `12 November 1993` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 this Act is barred from applying to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `1 January 1980` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Tests -- section 1`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The parenthesis names two effects of the 1874 Act.
#ASSERT count `s 1 the effects the Act describes the Infants Relief Act 1874 as having` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT elem `invalidating certain contracts made by minors` `s 1 the effects the Act describes the Infants Relief Act 1874 as having`
#ASSERT elem `prohibiting actions to enforce contracts ratified after majority` `s 1 the effects the Act describes the Infants Relief Act 1874 as having`

-- The scope: a contract made by a minor after 9 April 1987.
#ASSERT `s 1 the contract was made by a minor after 9 April 1987` (`the standard contract made on` `10 April 1987` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 1 the contract was made by a minor after 9 April 1987` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 the contract was made by a minor after 9 April 1987` (`the standard contract made on` `9 April 1987` NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1 the contract was made by a minor after 9 April 1987` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING))

-- The disapplication reaches a minor's contract made on or after 12 November 1993 (s 4 does not speak).
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `12 November 1993` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not made by a minor, the date met: s 1 says nothing (scope limit, no "only").
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Made on or before 9 April 1987: the date is fixed in the text's own words, so the disapplication does not reach the contract (FORK F2).
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `9 April 1987` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `1 January 1980` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Both failing: the date is tested before the minor limb (FORK F2).
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`a contract with` `9 April 1987` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In the band, with the exception not met, s 4 shuts s 1 out: the text says no.
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `10 April 1987` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `11 November 1993` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4 shuts out the whole Act, so it shuts s 1 out even for a contract s 1's own scope would have missed.
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`a contract with` `15 June 1990` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In the band with the exception met: the section's own words operate (QA (NOTES.md, Judgment calls)).  Not known: the text does not answer.
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the disapplication reaches the contract` (`a contract with` `15 June 1990` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Does the 1874 Act apply?  JUST FALSE only where s 1 reaches the contract.
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 applies to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 applies to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `12 November 1993` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 applies to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 applies to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 applies to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 applies to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `9 April 1987` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 applies to the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `1 January 1980` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 applies to the contract` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The two effects the parenthesis names follow the same answer.
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidates the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidates the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `12 November 1993` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidates the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `1 January 1980` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidates the contract` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 bars an action on the contract ratified after majority` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 bars an action on the contract ratified after majority` (`the standard contract made on` `12 November 1993` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 bars an action on the contract ratified after majority` (`the standard contract made on` `9 April 1987` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1 the Infants Relief Act 1874 bars an action on the contract ratified after majority` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Tests -- section 2`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Limb (a): a guarantee is given, in respect of an obligation under a contract made after 9 April 1987.
#ASSERT `s 2(a) a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to a contract made after 9 April 1987` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `10 April 1987` NOTHING) TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 2(a) a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to a contract made after 9 April 1987` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(a) a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to a contract made after 9 April 1987` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `9 April 1987` NOTHING) TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(a) a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to a contract made after 9 April 1987` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `1 January 1980` NOTHING) TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2(a) a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to a contract made after 9 April 1987` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) FALSE))

-- Limb (b), FORK F1: "because he was a minor" governs both limbs.  (unenforceable, repudiates, because) -> limb met?
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- unenforceable for another reason (not minority): not met
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- repudiated for another reason: not met on the reading taken (the other reading of F1 would say met)
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Limb (b) when the person does not know the law the Act presupposes: NOTHING, unless the facts that are known decide it.
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` NOTHING FALSE (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` NOTHING TRUE (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` (JUST FALSE) FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` NOTHING FALSE (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Limb (b) reads the record's minority fact first: when no party was a minor, "because he was a minor" cannot hold.
-- Not a minor, reason not known: JUST FALSE.  A minor, reason not known: NOTHING (as before).  A minor, reason yes: JUST TRUE (as before).
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract where the reason is not known and minority is` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract where the reason is not known and minority is` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a minor but the reason is given as minority, or the party repudiates: still not met, because the record says no party was a minor.
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(b) the obligation is unenforceable against him, or he repudiates the contract, because he was a minor when the contract was made` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Through the whole section: not a minor, reason not known: the section does not save the guarantee.
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract where the reason is not known and minority is` FALSE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract where the reason is not known and minority is` TRUE) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The decision.  All met, s 4 not speaking: the guarantee is saved.
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `12 November 1993` NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A contract that repudiates (second limb of (b)) is also within s 2.
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) fails: no guarantee given.
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) fails: contract made on or before 9 April 1987.
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `9 April 1987` NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `1 January 1980` NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) fails: neither limb, or for another reason.
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract with` `1 March 2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In the band, exception not met: s 4 shuts s 2 out.
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST FALSE)) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `10 April 1987` (JUST FALSE)) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `11 November 1993` (JUST FALSE)) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In the band, all else met: exception met, the section's own words operate and the guarantee is saved (QA (NOTES.md, Judgment calls)); exception not known, the text does not answer.
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST TRUE)) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `10 April 1987` (JUST TRUE)) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `11 November 1993` (JUST TRUE)) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- In the band, exception met, but the "where" fails on its own: JUST FALSE (fork F8: a failed own "where" is tested before an unknown exception).
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `15 June 1990` (JUST TRUE)) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract with` `15 June 1990` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The law the Act presupposes is not known: NOTHING, but a failed "where" or s 4's bar still says no.
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` NOTHING FALSE (JUST TRUE)) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract where the law presupposed is` (JUST FALSE) FALSE NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`a contract with` `15 June 1990` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE)) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is saved from unenforceability on that ground alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`Contract with a minor` WITH `day the contract was made` IS `15 June 1990`, `one party was a minor when the contract was made` IS TRUE, `the obligation is unenforceable against that party` IS NOTHING, `that party repudiates the contract` IS FALSE, `that is because that party was a minor when the contract was made` IS NOTHING, `section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made the provision applicable` IS (JUST TRUE)) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The tail: "the guarantee shall not for that reason alone be unenforceable against the guarantor".
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is unenforceable against the guarantor for that reason alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `1 March 2020` NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2 the guarantee is unenforceable against the guarantor for that reason alone` (`a guarantee case on` (`the standard contract made on` `12 November 1993` NOTHING) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where s 2 does not save the guarantee, it says nothing about its enforceability.
